$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Methyl
2-(3-Thiophenyl-2-oxoquinoxalin-1(2H)-yl)acetate Derivatives (12). A
mixture of K2CO3 (139 mg, 1 mmol) and phenol or phenthiol (1.1 mmol) in
DMF (10 mL) was stirred at 85 °C for 12 h. Then
2-(3-chloro-2-oxoquinoxalin-1(2H)-yl)acetate derivative 2 (1 mmol) was
added. The reaction mixture was stirred at 75 °C for 12 h and cooled to
room temperature. Then H2O (100 mL) was added, and the residue was
filtered off and washed with H2O to give the resulting residue, which was
purified by column chromatography to provide the desired product 12.
Methyl 2-(3-(4-Bromothiophenoxy)-2-oxoquinoxalin-1(2H)-yl)-acetate (12c).
Yield: 302 mg (75%); white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 7.73 (dd,
J = 8.4, 1.9 Hz, 2H), 7.58 (dd, J = 8.5, 1.9 Hz, 2H), 7.52 (d, J = 5.7
Hz, 2H), 7.35-7.27 (m, 2H), 5.17 (s, 2H), 3.72 ppm (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
